3. Introduction

A static website contains files such as HTML, CSS, and JavaScript that can be served without a server-side application.

CI/CD stands for Continuous Integration and Continuous Deployment. GitHub Actions can automatically build and deploy a website when changes are pushed to a repository.

GitHub Pages is a hosting service that publishes static websites directly from a GitHub repository.

